# Current events in town, part six: the same news in many more mouths. Region groups, seasons, weather, hours, and the
# bands between the two speaking.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Crime across the country

scene et_cr_country_theft
when topic=crime topic.kind=theft here.region=countryside
a : A thief, out here. We all know each other's doors. | #topic.victim# robbed, and the nearest watch is a day's ride. | Out here a theft's everybody's business.
b[farmer] : Then everybody'd better keep their eyes open.
b : Someone knew the door, then. | We'll be our own watch. | Always has been.
a : That's what worries me. | Again. | Always.

scene et_cr_city_theft
when topic=crime topic.kind=theft here.region=cities
a : Another one robbed. #topic.victim#. You stop counting in a city. | City thieves are quick as eels. #topic.victim# never felt a thing. | #topic.victim# was robbed in the crowd by the hall.
b[guard] : Crowds are their meat. Keep your coin in front of you.
b : Stop counting, stop caring. | Eels in a barrel. | Every crowd has a thief in it.
a : I try not to. | Slippery. | Or three.

scene et_cr_coast_theft
when topic=crime topic.kind=theft here.region=rain_coast
a : Somebody went through the smokehouse in the night. | Rain covers footsteps. #topic.victim# heard nothing. | Wet night, light fingers. #topic.victim# lost a purse.
b[fisher] : Rain's a thief's cloak on this coast.
b : The smell'll give them away. | It covers everything. | Always is, here.
a : You'd hope. | Everything. | Always.

scene et_cr_south_assault
when topic=crime topic.kind=assault here.region=south
a : Hot nights make hot tempers. #topic.victim# paid for someone's. | #topic.victim# got knifed in a quarrel over nothing. | They say it was the heat. Like that excuses it.
b[old] : Same every summer. The heat gets in the blood.
b : Paid dear. | Nothing's always worth killing over, isn't it. | It doesn't.
a : Too dear. | Apparently. | Not ever.

scene et_cr_north_arrest
when topic=crime topic.kind=arrest here.region=mountains
a : They marched #topic.subject# through the snow to the cells. | #topic.subject#'s arrested. They'll have a cold night. | Cells up here have frost on the inside. #topic.subject#'ll learn.
b[guard] : Cold cells make for quick confessions.
b : Snow and chains. Grim. | Good. | Hard lesson.
a : Very grim. | Fitting. | Hard country.

scene et_cr_fog_theft
when topic=crime topic.kind=theft here.weather=fog
a : The fog was so thick last night, a thief could walk in your front door. | #topic.victim# was robbed in the fog. Couldn't see a paw in front. | Fog like this is a gift for thieves.
b[guard] : We walked into each other twice on the round.
b : One did. Into #topic.victim#'s. | Who could? | And for ghosts.
a : Exactly. | Nobody. | Don't.

scene et_cr_storm_assault
when topic=crime topic.kind=assault here.weather=storm|rain
a : Nobody heard #topic.victim# shout over the storm. | #topic.victim# was set on in the rain. Nobody about. | Even the watch sheltered last night. That's when it happened to #topic.victim#.
b[guard] : We don't shelter. We... took a moment under the arch.
b : The storm drowned it. | Rain empties the streets. | Of course.
a : Poor soul. | It does. | Of course it did.

scene et_cr_rest_day
when topic=crime topic.kind=theft|assault here.day=rest
a : On a Restday, too. The Bright One's day. | Couldn't even keep the Restday holy. | Everyone at chapel, houses empty. That's when they struck.
b[priest] : Restday or no, the Dark One doesn't keep the calendar.
b : Nothing's sacred. | Not any more. | Clever and wicked.
a : Nothing. | Not for them. | Wicked.

scene et_cr_market_day
when topic=crime topic.kind=theft|assault here.day=market
a : Market day's always worst for thieves. | Half the country in the square, and someone's purse is lighter. | Busy market, busy pickpockets.
b[merchant] : I count my coin every hour on market day.
b : Always. | Usually mine. | Busy everything.
a : Every week. | Keep it closer. | Every week.

scene et_cr_dawn_found
when topic=crime topic.kind=assault here.time=dawn
a : Bakers found #topic.victim# at first light. | The dawn bell, and the shouting started. #topic.victim#. | First light showed the blood. #topic.victim#'s.
b[baker] : I'll never walk that lane at dawn without seeing it.
b : Grim way to start a day. | Heard the shouting. Thought it was a fire. | Awful.
a : Grim. | Worse than a fire. | Awful.

scene et_cr_rivals_blame
when topic=crime topic.kind=theft pair.band=rivals
a : Funny how you're the only one on the street not robbed. | Odd, isn't it, #topic.victim# robbed and you with a new coat. | Where were you the night #topic.victim# was robbed?
b : Funny how you'd think that. | I earned this coat. | Asleep. Like honest wolves.
a : Just saying. | I'm sure. | Of course.

scene et_cr_spouses_worry
when topic=crime topic.kind=theft|assault pair.band=spouses
a : Bolt the door tonight. I mean it. | We'll keep the coin under the hearthstone from now on. | I'm frightened. Is that foolish?
b : Bolted. And barred. | And I'll sit on the hearthstone. | No. I'm frightened too.
a : Good. | Idiot. | Good. Not just me.

scene et_cr_friends_walk
when topic=crime topic.kind=theft|assault pair.band=friends here.time=dusk|night
a : Walk me home? After what's been happening? | I'll go the long way, by the lamps. | Don't go down the back lane tonight.
b : Course. | I'll come with you. | I won't.
a : Thank you. | Thank you. | Promise.

scene et_cr_child_guard
when topic=crime topic.kind=theft|assault a.stage=young|adolescent b.role=guard
a : Did you catch the bad wolf yet? | Can I help catch the robber? | Are you going to fight the thief?
b : Not yet, pup. | You can keep your eyes open. That's helping. | Only if they're very foolish.
a : Hurry up! | I'll watch everything! | I hope they are.

scene et_cr_old_female
when topic=crime topic.kind=theft|assault a.stage=old a.sex=female
a : I keep my rolling pin by the door now. I'm not afraid to use it. | My mother kept the town's peace with a broom. I've still got it. | No thief's getting past me. I sleep like a cat.
b : I believe you. | I believe that too. | Lightly?
a : Good. | Very sturdy broom. | With one eye open.

scene et_cr_adolescent_bravado
when topic=crime topic.kind=theft|assault a.stage=adolescent pair.band=friends
a : If I'd been there, I'd have chased them off. | I could catch that thief. I'm fast. | Bet I could find who did it before the watch.
b : You'd have run the other way. | Faster than a blade? | You'd find trouble.
a : Would not. | Probably. | Same thing.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Lives across the country

scene et_lf_country_wedding
when topic=life topic.kind=marriage here.region=countryside
a : The whole valley's coming to #topic.subject#'s wedding. | Barn's swept for #topic.subject#'s wedding dance. | #topic.subject#'s wedding. Three days of eating.
b[farmer] : Wedding in the barn, sleeping in the hay. Proper country.
b : As it should be. | I'll bring the cider. | Three days! I'll need new trousers.
a : Always. | Good. | Bigger ones.

scene et_lf_city_wedding
when topic=life topic.kind=marriage here.region=cities
a : #topic.subject#'s wedding procession blocked the whole street. | #topic.subject# married at the big chapel. Very grand. | Did you see #topic.subject#'s wedding? Rose petals everywhere.
b[merchant] : Grand for them. Bad for my trade, with the street closed.
b : I was stuck behind it for an hour. | Grand and dear. | Still picking them out of my fur.
a : Worth it, though. | Very dear. | Lovely.

scene et_lf_north_death
when topic=life topic.kind=death here.region=mountains here.season=winter|autumn
a : They'll keep #topic.subject# cold till the ground softens. | Winter's long up here. #topic.subject# didn't see the end of it. | #topic.subject#'s gone. The cold took them, in the end.
b[old] : Cold's merciful, in its way. You just go to sleep.
b : The ground's like iron. | Too long. | It takes the old ones.
a : Iron. | Always too long. | And not only old.

scene et_lf_south_death
when topic=life topic.kind=death here.region=south
a : They'll bury #topic.subject# quick, with the heat. | Sun-sickness, they say. #topic.subject#. | #topic.subject# went in the hot spell.
b[priest] : Quick or slow, the Bright One waits the same.
b : Has to be. | Cruel sun. | Poor soul.
a : Has to be. | Cruel. | Poor soul.

scene et_lf_birth_winter
when topic=life topic.kind=birth here.season=winter
a : A winter pup for #topic.subject#. Born in the snow. | #topic.subject#'s pup came on the coldest night of the year. | Winter-born, #topic.subject#'s pup. Tough as old boots, they'll be.
b[old] : Winter pups are hardy. Spring pups are lucky. That's the saying.
b : Keep it warm! | Strong, then. | Tough as their mother.
a : They are. | Very strong. | Tougher.

scene et_lf_birth_spouses
when topic=life topic.kind=birth pair.band=spouses
a : #topic.subject#'s pups are so small. Do you ever think... | Did you see #topic.subject# with the pups? So happy. | #topic.subject#'s pups made me want our own.
b : I think about it all the time. | Happy and exhausted. | Me too.
a : Really? | Both. | Then maybe.

scene et_lf_appr_country
when topic=life topic.kind=apprentice here.region=countryside|towns
a : #topic.subject#'s going off to apprentice in the city. | #topic.subject#'s apprenticed to the smith here. Stayed home. | #topic.subject# starts with the miller tomorrow.
b : The city swallows them. | Good. We need trades here. | Flour to the ears by noon.
a : It might. | We do. | Ha.

scene et_lf_appr_rivals
when topic=life topic.kind=apprentice pair.band=rivals
a : #topic.subject# got the apprenticeship you wanted. | Did you hear who got taken on? #topic.subject#. Not you. | Shame about the apprenticeship. #topic.subject#'s, not yours.
b : I didn't want it. | I'm aware. | You're enjoying this.
a : Course not. | Just checking. | A little.

scene et_lf_succ_rivals
when topic=life topic.kind=succession pair.band=rivals
a : #topic.subject# takes over, and you get nothing. Again. | Passed over for #topic.subject#. How does that feel? | #topic.subject# got it all. Your face!
b : Feels like I'll be fine. | Wonderful, thanks. | Enjoy it while it lasts.
a : Sure. | Ha. | I will.

scene et_lf_succ_old
when topic=life topic.kind=succession a.stage=old
a : #topic.subject# has the running of it now. In my day, you waited till the old one died. | Young #topic.subject# in charge. The world goes too fast. | #topic.subject# took over. I gave my trade over too late, myself.
b : Times change. | Too fast. | Better too late than too early.
a : Not for the better. | Much too fast. | Is it?

scene et_lf_death_guard_b
when topic=life topic.kind=death b.role=guard
a : Did you know #topic.subject#? | Will the watch be at #topic.subject#'s burying? | They say you found #topic.subject#.
b : A little. Good sort. | All of us. | I did. I'd rather not talk about it.
a : I'm sorry. | Good. | Of course.

scene et_lf_death_child_b
when topic=life topic.kind=death b.stage=young|adolescent
a : You're very quiet. Is it about #topic.subject#? | It's all right to be sad about #topic.subject#. | Do you want to talk about #topic.subject#?
b : I keep thinking about them. | I know. | No.
a : That's how you remember them. | Good. | All right. I'm here.

scene et_lf_marriage_old_couple
when topic=life topic.kind=marriage a.stage=old b.stage=old
a : #topic.subject#'s married. Remember our wedding? | #topic.subject# wed today. We were that young once. | Watching #topic.subject# marry made me cry like a pup.
b : I remember you trod on my tail. | Younger. Foolish. | You always cry.
a : Once. | Happy fools. | Only at weddings.

scene et_lf_marriage_merchant_b
when topic=life topic.kind=marriage b.role=merchant
a : #topic.subject#'s wedding. Did you sell them anything? | Who did the wedding cloth for #topic.subject#? | #topic.subject#'s getting married. I need a gift.
b : Half the feast. | I did. Finest weave. | I've just the thing.
a : Good for you. | It was fine. | Of course you have.

scene et_lf_newcomer_marriage
when topic=life topic.kind=marriage pair.band=acquaintances
a : #topic.subject#'s wedding was something. | Did you go to #topic.subject#'s wedding? | #topic.subject# married. Nice day for it.
b : I heard. | No. Wasn't asked. | Wasn't it.
a : It was. | Nor me. | Lovely.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Newcomers across the country

scene et_nc_city_crowd
when topic=newcomer here.region=cities
a : Another newcomer. #topic.subject#. The city swallows them by the dozen. | #topic.subject#'s new. You can tell by how they flinch at carts. | Saw #topic.subject# lost in the market. City's too big for them.
b[official] : Have them register at the City Office. Everyone registers.
b : And spits most of them out. | We all flinched once. | It's too big for me.
a : Usually. | I still do. | Me too.

scene et_nc_towns
when topic=newcomer here.region=towns
a : A newcomer here's news for a week. #topic.subject#. | #topic.subject# came to stay. In this town. | Everyone's had a look at #topic.subject# by now.
b : More than a week. | Wonder why. | Poor thing. Like a show.
a : A month. | We'll find out. | Every eye.

scene et_nc_winter_arrival
when topic=newcomer here.season=winter
a : Who arrives in winter? #topic.subject#, apparently. | #topic.subject# came in half-frozen. | Strange time to move, winter. #topic.subject# did.
b[innkeeper] : I gave them the room by the chimney.
b : Someone with no choice. | Poor thing. | Running from something.
a : That's what worries me. | Thawing now. | Probably.

scene et_nc_spring_arrival
when topic=newcomer here.season=spring|summer
a : #topic.subject# came with the warm weather. | New faces every #here.season#. #topic.subject# this time. | #topic.subject# arrived with the swallows.
b : Sensible. | Every year. | Will they leave with them?
a : Very. | Some stay. | We'll see.

scene et_nc_rivals
when topic=newcomer pair.band=rivals
a : I suppose you've already made friends with #topic.subject#. | #topic.subject# seems to like you. No accounting for taste. | Don't go poisoning #topic.subject# against me.
b : Somebody has to be friendly. | Jealous? | I'll tell them the truth.
a : Charming. | Never. | That's what I'm afraid of.

scene et_nc_spouses
when topic=newcomer pair.band=spouses
a : Was #topic.subject# looking at you at chapel? | #topic.subject#'s handsome, isn't he? Don't answer that. | We should have #topic.subject# round. They're alone.
b : Only you, love. | I won't. | Good idea.
a : Hm. | Good. | Tomorrow, then.

scene et_nc_old_female
when topic=newcomer a.stage=old a.sex=female
a : I'll take that #topic.subject# a pot of broth. Too thin, that one. | #topic.subject# needs feeding up. I'll see to it. | That newcomer #topic.subject# has no one to mend for them.
b : They'll thank you. | Feeding up, aye. | Bless you.
a : Course they will. | I'll start tonight. | Somebody must.

scene et_nc_child_friend
when topic=newcomer a.stage=young b.stage=young
a : The new wolf #topic.subject# has a pup our age! | #topic.subject#'s pup is new. Can they play with us? | #topic.subject# gave me a sweet!
b : Can we play with them? | They can be on my side. | Did you share it?
a : Let's ask! | My side! | No.

scene et_nc_carter
when topic=newcomer b.job=carter
a : Did you bring #topic.subject# in your wagon? | #topic.subject# came with your load, didn't they? | #topic.subject# said you gave them a ride.
b : Picked them up on the road. Sore feet. | They paid with a song. Badly. | I did. Talked the whole way.
a : Kind of you. | Ha. | That's the price.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Festivals across the country

scene et_fs_city
when topic=festival here.region=cities topic.when=today
a : The streets are so full for #here.festival# you can't move. | Music on every corner for #here.festival#. | The hall's lit up for #here.festival#.
b[guard] : Every pickpocket in the country's here too.
b : Squeeze through. | Pick a corner. | Like a lantern.
a : Squeezing. | All of them. | Beautiful.

scene et_fs_towns
when topic=festival here.region=towns|countryside topic.when=today
a : Everyone's on the green for #here.festival#. | One fiddler, one drum, the whole town dancing. For #here.festival#. | Trestle tables down the street for #here.festival#.
b[old] : Same green, same tunes, sixty years. Wouldn't change a thing.
b : Even the miser came. | Best kind. | Pass the bread.
a : Even him. | The best. | Here.

scene et_fs_rain
when topic=festival topic.when=soon here.weather=rain|storm|fog
a : If this weather holds, #here.festival# will be a washout. | Pray it clears for #here.festival#. | Rain all week. Bad sign for #here.festival#.
b[priest] : I'll pray. The Bright One owes us a fine day.
b : It'll clear. | Praying. | Signs are nonsense.
a : I hope. | Good. | Hope so.

scene et_fs_snow
when topic=festival here.weather=snow
a : Snow for #here.festival#! Perfect. | Bonfire in the snow for #here.festival#. | Fresh snow, ribbons, it's #here.festival#.
b[child] : Snowball fight at #here.festival#! I've got a pile ready!
b : Prettiest feast day. | Warm in front, cold behind. | Couldn't be better.
a : Prettiest. | Turn around now and then. | Couldn't.

scene et_fs_spouses
when topic=festival pair.band=spouses topic.when=soon
a : What shall we bring to #here.festival#? | Shall we dance at #here.festival# like we used to? | Wear the green for #here.festival#. For me.
b : The plum cake. Always. | My knees say no. My heart says yes. | For you, anything.
a : Always. | Listen to your heart. | Good.

scene et_fs_friends
when topic=festival pair.band=friends topic.when=today
a : Come on! It's #here.festival#! Stop working! | Meet me by the bonfire for #here.festival#. | Let's get a pie and watch the dancers for #here.festival#.
b : Just finishing. | I'll find you. | Two pies.
a : Now! | Don't be late. | Three.

scene et_fs_rivals
when topic=festival pair.band=rivals topic.when=soon
a : I suppose you'll be showing off at #here.festival# again. | Don't steal my place at the #here.festival# table this year. | Your pie won the prize at #here.festival#. Fluke.
b : I don't show off. | It's not your place. | Skill.
a : Ha. | It is. | Fluke.

scene et_fs_adolescent
when topic=festival a.stage=adolescent
a : Do you think anyone will ask me to dance at #here.festival#? | I'm staying up all night for #here.festival#. Nobody can stop me. | Can I have a cup of ale at #here.festival#? Just one?
b : Someone will. | We'll see. | Half a cup.
a : Who? | We will. | Half!

scene et_fs_old_male
when topic=festival a.stage=old a.sex=male
a : I'll be telling my stories at #here.festival#, whether they want them or not. | I won the arm wrestling at #here.festival# six years running. Once. | My voice is going, but I'll sing at #here.festival#.
b : They always want them. | Six years running, once? | We'll all sing with you.
a : They don't. | Close enough. | Good.

scene et_fs_merchant_b
when topic=festival b.role=merchant topic.when=soon
a : Will you set up a stall for #here.festival#? | What are you selling at #here.festival#? | Busy week for you, with #here.festival#.
b : Two stalls. | Sweets, ribbons, anything shiny. | The busiest.
a : Greedy. | Shiny sells. | Good.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Gossip across the country

scene et_gs_city
when topic=gossip here.region=cities
a : Everyone in the city's heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | In the city you can't sneeze without everyone knowing. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | It's on every corner. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : The city's a big mouth. | Bless you. | Every corner.
a : Biggest there is. | Ha. | Every one.

scene et_gs_country
when topic=gossip here.region=countryside|towns
a : Out here there's nothing to do but talk. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Small town, big ears. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Everyone knows. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : And talk we do. | Huge ears. | Course they do.
a : Endlessly. | Enormous. | Always.

scene et_gs_rain
when topic=gossip here.weather=rain|fog|snow
a : Nothing to do in this weather but talk. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Stuck indoors, and I heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Under the eaves: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : The weather breeds gossip. | Indoors is where gossip lives. | Eaves hear everything.
a : It does. | Always. | Everything.

scene et_gs_adolescent
when topic=gossip a.stage=adolescent b.stage=adolescent
a : You'll never believe it. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#! | Swear you won't tell. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Everyone at the well says #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : I believe anything. | Swear. | Everyone!
a : Ha! | Good. | Everyone.

scene et_gs_old_pair
when topic=gossip a.stage=old b.stage=old
a : We're too old for gossip. But #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Did your hearing catch this one? #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | In our day, a wolf who #topic.claim# hid for a year. Now #topic.subject# struts about.
b : Too old to stop. | Louder. | Different times.
a : Much too old. | #topic.subject# #topic.claim#! | Worse times.

scene et_gs_merchant_pair
when topic=gossip a.role=merchant b.role=merchant
a : Between stalls: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Customer told me #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Heard at the scales: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : Bad for their credit. | Customers talk. | Scales don't lie, folk do.
a : Very bad. | All day. | True.

scene et_gs_apprentice
when topic=gossip pair.band=apprentice
a : Master, is it true #topic.subject# #topic.claim#? | The other apprentices say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | I heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#, master.
b : Sweep, don't gossip. | The other apprentices talk too much. | Back to work.
a : Yes, master. | Sorry, master. | Yes, master.

scene et_gs_guard_pair
when topic=gossip a.role=guard b.role=guard
a : Off the record. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Watch house talk: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | The captain thinks #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : Off the record, I heard that too. | Watch house talks more than a market. | The captain thinks a lot of things.
a : Interesting. | Much more. | Mostly wrong.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- News across the country

scene et_nw_rivals
when topic=news pair.band=rivals
a : Before you hear it wrong: #topic.news#. | Thought I'd tell you myself. #topic.news#. | #topic.news#. Go on, gloat.
b : Thanks for telling me. | That's decent of you. | I won't gloat.
a : Don't make it a habit. | I can be. | That's a first.

scene et_nw_old
when topic=news a.stage=old
a : At my age, news is rare. #topic.news#. | Listen, before I forget. #topic.news#. | #topic.news#. Still surprises in me yet.
b : Rare and good. | I'm listening. | Plenty, I'd say.
a : Very rare. | Good. | Ha.

scene et_nw_spouses
when topic=news pair.band=spouses
a : I didn't know how to tell you. #topic.news#. | Sit down, love. #topic.news#. | You'll hear it at the well, so here. #topic.news#.
b : We'll face it together. | Sitting. | Thank you for telling me first.
a : Together. | Good. | Always first.

scene et_nw_tavern
when topic=news here.place=tavern
a : Buy me a drink, I've news. #topic.news#. | #topic.news#. That's worth a cup. | Here's my news, and then I'm drinking. #topic.news#.
b[innkeeper] : That's worth one on the house.
b : Drinks are on me. | Worth two. | Drink, then.
a : Thank you. | Two! | Gladly.

scene et_nw_strangers
when topic=news pair.band=strangers
a : Odd thing to tell a stranger, but #topic.news#. | You don't know me, but #topic.news#. | #topic.news#. Sorry, I needed to tell someone.
b : Sometimes a stranger's easiest. | I'm glad you did. | It's all right.
a : It is. | Thank you. | Thank you.
